+````markdown name=ops/k8s/vault_csi.md
+```text
+Vault CSI (Secrets Store CSI Driver) integration notes (defaults used)
+
+Assumptions:
+ - You have HashiCorp Vault deployed and reachable at VAULT_ADDR.
+ - You have installed the Secrets Store CSI Driver + Vault provider in your cluster.
+ - This doc shows a minimal SecretProviderClass example to mount secrets into pods (not a production-ready RBAC policy).
+
+Example SecretProviderClass (adapt to your cluster):
+
+apiVersion: secrets-store.csi.x-k8s.io/v1
+kind: SecretProviderClass
+metadata:
+  name: aegis-vault-spc
+  namespace: aegis
+spec:
+  provider: vault
+  secretObjects:
+    - secretName: aegis-core-secrets
+      type: Opaque
+      data:
+        - objectName: "secret/data/aegis/core#MLFLOW_DB_URL"
+          key: MLFLOW_DB_URL
+        - objectName: "secret/data/aegis/core#EVIDENCE_BUCKET"
+          key: EVIDENCE_BUCKET
+  parameters:
+    vaultAddress: "{{ VAULT_ADDR }}"
+    roleName: "aegis-k8s-role"
+    objects: |
+      - objectName: "secret/data/aegis/core#MLFLOW_DB_URL"
+      - objectName: "secret/data/aegis/core#EVIDENCE_BUCKET"
+
+Deploy:
+ - Install Secrets Store CSI Driver and Vault provider:
+     https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/secrets-store-csi-driver
+ - Create Kubernetes ServiceAccount and Vault role binding (use OIDC/workload identity pattern)
+ - Create SecretProviderClass and update workloads to mount provider secrets
+
+Security:
+ - Do not store long-lived credentials in k8s secrets; use Vault with short-lived tokens.
+ - Limit RBAC for ServiceAccounts that use the SecretProviderClass.
+````
